#: f50a82ae013844819ee595c5c9cc3b83
msgid "SERIAL4 -> UART6 (RCIN port)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:39
#: d44e389000c342238533f2a75f62de91
msgid "SERIAL5 -> UART7 (debug)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:41
#: 2781528631a742dfbdc684ee4ebddff3
msgid "The SERIAL1 port has RTS/CTS pins, the other UARTs do not have RTS/CTS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:43
#: dc13421af4eb4f63b1232291c16023db
msgid "The RCIN port can be used as RX or TX as a general UART using the SERIAL4_OPTIONS bits to swap pins. It is not used for RC input (the PPM pin is used for RC input)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:47
#: bb41276137314836a4309eed7c080d59
msgid "The UART7 connector is inside the case and labelled as debug, but is available as a general purpose UART with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:51
#: 678d080aa1af421aa69e2ee421675f78
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:52
#: a42a88cfe5c143c0bc1818c7f962c6e8
msgid "The PPM pin, which by default is mapped to a timer input, can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:54
#: 1b77ec71cfbe4696b6ed08ef38bca6b9
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the RCIN port's RCIN pin can also be configured to be used as true UART RX or TX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the SERIAL4 parameters appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:56
#: fc990d677a0f4254912b783e6b91278d
msgid "To use RCIN for bi-directional RC and Telemetry protocols, :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL<SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:58
#: aeda3dd62bd644b68f2245c93f5f42af
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:60
#: 13f2354c634844c5b552690158fa3f3e
msgid "SBUS/DSM/SRXL connects to the RCIN pin, but SBUS requires that the :ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS<SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` be set to \"3\" to invert the signal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:62
#: aa00babf6e354536912b02f6b1781952
msgid "FPort requires connection to RCIN and :ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS<SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` be set to \"15\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:64
#: 96a4bc7e62134ab59c8de2cd95c7ba95
msgid "CRSF requires connection to both RX and TX of a UART, so the RCIN port and pin cannot be used. Instead either SERIAL1 (UART2), SERIAL2 (UART4), or SERIAL3 (UART1 must be used. Set its protocol to \"23\" and options to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:66
#: dc5a980444494b819449a5ddf401e062
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to RCIN and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS<SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:68
#: 1d776558a0774f7289a6699cc97a3dbc
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:71
#: 6f5ff1996a934f5f93cdc33d22da23a6
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:73
#: 4077cd90f58b44d8b1b58556b7f41eb9
msgid "The Pixhawk4-Mini supports up to 11 PWM outputs. All 11 outputs support all normal PWM output formats. All outputs except numbers 7 and 8 support DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:77
#: cc60b0363f40444f9f28cd04fb225def
msgid "The first 8 outputs are labelled \"MAIN OUT\" on the case. The next 3 outputs are labelled CAP1 to CAP3 on the case. The CAP4 pin cannot be used as a PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:81
#: 00a73257560947fcb545091e06b75795
msgid "The 11 PWM outputs are in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:83
#: dc2ee3248e6c4ff1854a8bc166581a4b
msgid "PWM 1, 2, 3 and 4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:84
#: f9484893b2ba4cc190b84c34d1f110c5
msgid "PWM 5 and 6 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:85
#: e8a2d98b31744432ab7f6d62e9573f05
msgid "PWM 7 and 8 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:86
#: dd2e9199e280458eaf5a9b77120a1bdd
msgid "PWM 9, 10 and 11 in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:88
#: db875f7b08124d94ae9a4d27b9322ba4
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:93
#: 02581b10b25046ff8d8ce9e0f0fa032e
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:95
#: 127480750862417290789a17ec4299b4
msgid "The board has a dedicated power monitor port with a 6 pin connector. The correct battery setting parameters are dependent on the type of power module which is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:100
#: b154c220134149d19d0a5207eaef9268
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:102
#: cbbd4811a5d5443ebb98b33046bb8049
msgid "The Pixhawk4-Mini has a builtin IST8310 compass. Due to potential interference the board is usually used with an external I2C compass as part of a GPS/Compass combination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:107
#: 245c9fbf049d476e9f4f7cbcd57f643c
msgid "GPIOs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:109
#: 5fd75ebdfb2a435bb8b5603b1c00a41e
msgid "The 11 PWM ports plus the CAP4 ports can be used as GPIOs (relays, buttons, RPM etc). To use them you need to limit the number of these pins that is used for PWM by setting the BRD_PWM_COUNT to a number less than 11. See :ref:`common-gpios` page for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-ph4mini.rst:114
#: a2cd24f23a23448c9e5e0ebc0ad3bcec
msgid "For example if you set BRD_PWM_COUNT to 8 then CAP1, CAP2 and CAP3 will be available for use as GPIOs, in addition to CAP4."
msgstr ""

